WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.490
And finally, Jasper Cropsey's
Autumn on the Hudson River, 1860.

2
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.410
Gold light, blazing trees,
the river winding through a dream.

3
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.310
Beautiful, yes. But look closely,
and you'll find people:

4
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.570
small figures resting by a pond,
a village with a church spire, a bridge,

5
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.610
sailboats on the river.
The valley is settled, but only by newcomers.

6
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.130
The Lenape and Mohican peoples
of the Hudson Valley are nowhere to be seen.
